  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the Living Conditions of Affected Populations (IDPS and returnees) in the Central African Republic through Multi-Sectoral Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2013, the Central African Republic (CAR) has been affected by political, security and humanitarian crises linked to armed conflicts, inter-community conflicts or tensions between farmers and herders in certain areas, but also torrential rains and subsequent flooding during the rainy season. These conflicts, tensions and hazards caused the displacement of more than 500,000 persons in 2022 in the whole country. Through a multi-sectoral emergency response, IOM is contributing to improving the living conditions of conflict and non-conflict affected populations through: the deployment of the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM); distribution of Emergency Shelters and non-food item (NFI) kits; construction of transitional shelters and latrines; and support to returnees with basic skills training courses and Income Generating Activities.</narrative>
  </description>
